17. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Security is mandatory.

1. Do not expose GitHub PATs, Cloudflare API tokens, Resend keys, or other server secrets.
2. Do not add secrets to the frontend bundle or browser localStorage.
3. Validate all ad configuration data before saving.
4. Validate URLs and permitted provider formats.
5. Prevent arbitrary HTML/JavaScript from executing inside the Admin interface.
6. Do not use unsafe raw HTML rendering for untrusted strings.
7. Use controlled rendering for supported ad code.
8. Avoid script injection and DOM-based XSS.
9. Do not bypass Content Security Policy.
10. Preserve existing authentication, session validation, authorization, and admin permissions.
11. Only authorized administrators may modify ad settings.
12. Prevent unauthorized users from updating global ad status.
13. Handle invalid or malformed configurations safely.
14. Do not expose internal diagnostics, server errors, tokens, or secrets to public visitors.
15. Avoid loading third-party advertising scripts when ads are globally disabled.
16. Respect any existing consent-management behavior and applicable privacy controls.
17. Do not silently enable real ads or Google Auto Ads as part of the migration.
18. Preserve the existing AdSense publisher ID and integration settings only when already configured and valid.

If the current architecture cannot safely execute a particular ad format, reject that format with a clear explanation instead of weakening security.

